<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
          http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
          https://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.23.xsd">

    <!--
        Accumulated fouls on the event timeline - opt in, per tournament.

        Until now a foul was ONLY a counter (matches.fouls1_first &co): a
        running total per team per half, with no record of when any single foul
        happened. That is all the "deveterac" display needs, and it is why the
        timeline could not show fouls at all.

        From here a foul ALSO writes a FOUL row on match_events, stamped with
        the minute like every other timeline entry, so "3. accumulated foul in
        the 12th minute" becomes something the app can render. The counters stay
        the source of truth for the deveterac display - they are not derived
        from the events, so nothing about the existing zapisnik behaviour
        changes and no backfill is needed.

        Fouls recorded BEFORE this change have no events and therefore never
        appear on a timeline. Nothing can recover them: the information was
        never stored.

        The flag itself is per TOURNAMENT and off by default - most organizers
        do not want a timeline that is mostly fouls, and the players who asked
        for it are a minority of one tournament. Switching it off leaves the
        FOUL events in place; they are simply not rendered, so turning it back
        on shows the full history rather than only what happened since.
    -->
    <changeSet id="2026-08-04-01-tournaments-show-fouls-in-timeline" author="mrodek">
        <addColumn tableName="tournaments">
            <column name="show_fouls_in_timeline" type="boolean" defaultValueBoolean="false">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
